What is MAC Address?
Media Access Control (MAC) Address is a physical address of a device and unlike IP Address, MAC Address is unique and permanent.

What is MAC Spoofing?
Technique used to change the MAC Address of a network interface which originally assigned by the machine's factory

Why MAC Spoofing is done?
Change your device's identity, often used to impersonate someone's device to gain access to certain local networks by bypassing the MAC filtering.
Some hackers used it for Man-in-the-Middle Attack.
Ethical use includes changing the function of a computer from a router especially when only one public IP is available.

Prevention?
MAC Locking.
